Feature: The mesh
  A drone in a radio shadow can reach its team through a friend. A drone in a shadow is in
  contact if a drone of its team is within 70 m of it, flies, and is in contact itself. One drone
  can relay only for a drone that is in a shadow. A relayed drone relays for the next drone in
  the same way, so a chain of drones, each within 70 m of the one before, carries the radio into
  a shadow. The chain is at most 3 drones long, and it breaks where a drone is down, on the
  ground or out of range.

  Thus a drone at the edge of a shadow is a [[picket]]. A drone that circles a tower can never
  be relayed from outside the shadow, because the circle is wider than the gap. It must leave
  the circle to reach its team.

  Expectation: A drone in a shadow is in contact through a friend outside the shadow
    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is 150 m from the Red home tower
    And the second Blue drone is 210 m from the Red home tower
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is in contact

  Expectation: A friend that is in a shadow itself does not relay
    Overrides: A drone in a shadow is in contact through a friend outside the shadow
    Both drones are in the radio shadow, so neither one is in contact.

    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is 150 m from the Red home tower
    And the second Blue drone is 130 m from the Red home tower
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is cut

  Expectation: A friend more than 70 m away does not relay
    Overrides: A drone in a shadow is in contact through a friend outside the shadow
    The second Blue drone is outside the shadow, but 80 m from the first.

    Given the Red home tower is held by Red
    And the first Blue drone is 150 m from the Red home tower
    And the second Blue drone is 230 m from the Red home tower
    Then the link of the first Blue drone is cut
